// Ch6 B07 "Liss and the lantern" (act1_ch06.md; W14). In-engine. Rhen and Liss alone by the burning
// tide-wheel while Toma writes her into his papers. Asha is off-frame, with Toma (ADR 0022 sweep-G/I:
// no Act I line, bark or reaction has Asha connect the lantern to anyone), so she has no line here
// and stands at the papers table, out of W14. Liss reads Dace's work in a glance (the pair seat is
// sweep-H's: he built his lanterns as a pair); Rhen deflects. Do not surface: Rhen never says "my
// father was a wright" in Act I (admitted at Lowlight, Ch11).
title: ch06_liss_lantern
location: ch06/brine_shoals
---
@mark asha way_tents_e walk
@camera W14
@music liss_theme
@anim liss look_at rhen
Liss [neutral]: Hold still. That's a wright's housing. Pair-built: see the second seat, for the hook? #line:ch06_lantern_001
Liss [neutral]: And an oil burner in salt-glass. Who fits an oil burner in salt-glass? #line:ch06_lantern_002
<<if $ch02_rhen_named_lantern>>
    Rhen [neutral]: It was my father's. #line:ch06_lantern_003
    Liss [neutral]: Then your father bought from a wright. Or knew one. #line:ch06_lantern_004
    Rhen [neutral]: He knew a lot of people. #line:ch06_lantern_005
<<else>>
    Rhen [smile]: Somebody who liked oil. Good trade. #line:ch06_lantern_006
    Liss [neutral]: Nobody trades wright work that good. Somebody gave it up. #line:ch06_lantern_007
<<endif>>
@anim rhen look_at liss
@wait 0.8
Liss [cold]: You sell the dead by the pound, diver. At least I put them back to work. #line:ch06_lantern_008
<<set $ch06_liss_read_lantern = true>>
===
